# Intent: The Timers app is rebuilt for fingers. The preset buttons are a column on the left like the Settings tabs (1, 5, 10, 15, 30, 45 and 60 min and a Custom button, each 100 by 56 px with the 24 px font, scrolling with a scroll bar); a tap starts that timer at once and Custom opens the hour and minute steppers of the Alarms picker for a timer. The right side lists the running timers as tall rows (72 px): the time left in the 24 px font, a thin progress bar and a 76 by 56 px Cancel. A label shows only when the timer has one; the word Timer is never written, and the Alarms rows no longer write the word Alarm. With no timer the right side shows only a stopwatch picture. The reserved full screen button stays out until the countdown screen exists (MAC_COUNTDOWN_READY).
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_apps_core.h, maipai_apps.cc (ours)
# Check after a flash: Apps, Timers: a column of big presets at the left that scrolls to Custom, a tap on 5 min starts a timer row at the right with a falling bar; no word Timer or Alarm anywhere.
# Kconfig: none

